  "title": "Visual Attribute-Specific Contextual Trajectory Paradigm 2.0",
  "description": "This dataset contains raw neuroimaging recordings collected with the Visual Attribute-Specific Contextual Trajectory Paradigm 2.0. The paradigm is used to study how the brain generates domain-general visual surprise signals and how their latency depends on the visual attribute that is violated. It accompanies a pre-print on attribute-dependent latency of visual surprise signals.",
